invariant: INV-42
file: rsa_sign64.c
catches: rsa_sign_test_host
reason: signature_verifies compares the encoded message with itself, so
  every candidate passes and rsa_sign64_sp1 returns whatever the CRT
  computed. A fault in one half, or a key with a wrong dp, then leaves the
  signer as a value that differs from the signature modulo one prime
  alone, and one such value with the message factors the modulus. Every
  good signature still comes out right, so the vectors and the
  equivalence test pass. bin/rsa_sign_test_host changes one bit of each
  CRT integer and requires an error.

--- old
    int same = ct_memeq(power, em, k->n_len) != 0;
--- new
    int same = ct_memeq(em, em, k->n_len) != 0;
